    <item>
      <title>Patreon - Journal 2017-02-25</title>
      <link>/posts/patreon---journal-2017-02-25/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>/posts/patreon---journal-2017-02-25/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;From email 2017-02-25&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Hey everyone,&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The last few weeks have been incredibly turbulent. Between a mountain of chaos with school visits gone wrong, being knocked back for science communication work in Australia at the same time as incredible offers for work overseas, leading me to question whether I should keep trying to make a difference in my home country&amp;hellip; I&amp;rsquo;ve also had someone who I honestly never thought I&amp;rsquo;d see again come back into my life. And just as quickly as she reappeared, it now looks like she&amp;rsquo;ll disappear from it again. &lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Patreon - Post Visit Mars One Q&amp;A</title>
      <link>/posts/patreon---post-visit-mars-one-qa/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>/posts/patreon---post-visit-mars-one-qa/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;From email 2017-04-04&#xA;From &lt;a href=&#34;https://web.archive.org/web/20170617122035/http://joshrichards.space/category/personal/&#34;&gt;https://web.archive.org/web/20170617122035/http://joshrichards.space/category/personal/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;post-visit-mars-one-qa&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.patreon.com/posts/post-visit-mars-8677199?token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJyZWRpc19rZXkiOiJpbnN0YW50LWFjY2VzczpiMmE2YzZhNS1mYTY5LTQ0OGEtOWQyNC1kNWFhM2NmMmM3ZTgifQ.z4bBAzoX_6RwMD6l0n6OZsjf25dJmqy0_xrZKkp4nhk&amp;amp;utm_medium=post_notification_email&amp;amp;utm_campaign=patron_engagement&amp;amp;utm_source=post_link&#34;&gt;Post Visit Mars One Q&amp;amp;A&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;personal--mars-one-school-visit-qa&#34;&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://web.archive.org/web/20170617122035/http://joshrichards.space/2017/05/25/personal-mars-one-school-visit-qa/&#34; title=&#34;Permalink to Personal – Mars One School Visit Q&amp;amp;A&#34;&gt;Personal – Mars One School Visit Q&amp;amp;A&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://web.archive.org/web/20170617122035/http://joshrichards.space/2017/05/25/personal-mars-one-school-visit-qa/&#34; title=&#34;06:00&#34;&gt;May 25, 2017&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href=&#34;https://web.archive.org/web/20170617122035/http://joshrichards.space/author/hailsagan/&#34; title=&#34;View all posts by Josh&#34;&gt;Josh&lt;/a&gt;  Posted in &lt;a href=&#34;https://web.archive.org/web/20170617122035/http://joshrichards.space/category/personal/&#34;&gt;Personal&lt;/a&gt;  Tagged &lt;a href=&#34;https://web.archive.org/web/20170617122035/http://joshrichards.space/tag/hi-seas/&#34;&gt;Hi-SEAS&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://web.archive.org/web/20170617122035/http://joshrichards.space/tag/mars/&#34;&gt;mars&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://web.archive.org/web/20170617122035/http://joshrichards.space/tag/mars-one/&#34;&gt;mars one&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://web.archive.org/web/20170617122035/http://joshrichards.space/tag/psychology/&#34;&gt;Psychology&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://web.archive.org/web/20170617122035/http://joshrichards.space/tag/radiation/&#34;&gt;radiation&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://web.archive.org/web/20170617122035/http://joshrichards.space/tag/schools/&#34;&gt;schools&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://web.archive.org/web/20170617122035/http://joshrichards.space/tag/science/&#34;&gt;science&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://web.archive.org/web/20170617122035/http://joshrichards.space/tag/space/&#34;&gt;space&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://web.archive.org/web/20170617122035/http://joshrichards.space/tag/speaking/&#34;&gt;speaking&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&#34;https://web.archive.org/web/20170617122035/http://joshrichards.space/tag/the-martian/&#34;&gt;The Martian&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://web.archive.org/web/20170617122035im_/https://i2.wp.com/joshrichards.space/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/scicomm.jpg?resize=400%2C267&#34; alt=&#34;&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I wanted to share something that happens when you regularly visit schools and talk about something awesome like exploring Mars: the job isn’t just answering questions for kids at the school on the day, it also usually means answering questions for kids (and adults) who couldn’t make it or didn’t have time to ask their question on the day too!&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
